    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0747" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.00/513.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Bundy to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> with Government’s commission of inquiry, of
                    which General Receiver is a member, has been at Sinoe since November 10.
                    Commander wires me today that tribes refuse peace and fighting is beginning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
